## DESCRIPTION
## Higher order derivatives
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Higher order derivatives')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML


Here you will practice quick computations with multi-index notation. Sometimes you will take advantage of a nice property or pattern. Take a moment to think about what makes them simple.

(1). Compute [` \partial^{(1,2,3)}(2x^3 + 3y+5z^2+7xyz+11x^2y^2z^2 + 13yz^3) `].

[________]{Real(0)}

(2). Compute [` \partial^{(1,2,3)}( xy^2z^3) `].

[________]{Real(12)}

(3). Compute [` \partial^{(1,2,3)}(x^3y^2z + x^2yz^3 + xy^3z^2+ xy^2z^3) `].

[________]{Real(12)}
END_PGML

$showHint = 1;
BEGIN_HINT
$BR
Figure out ways to use linearity and Clairaut’s theorem to minimize work.
END_HINT

################################################################
#
#  Answers

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
BEGIN_SOLUTION
$BR
1. If you take the derivative with respect to \(z\) three times you see that only the last term remains. Further taking an \(x\) derivative on that term will give \(0\).
END_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();